Potuz: I it's

11
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:40.410
Potuz: So, when we remove this partial state transition on 5094, That happened when we import the payload, then we…

12
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:46.370
Potuz: We… We have… we moved into the system in which the block

13
00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:54.969
Potuz: processes the requests at the beginning from the previous payload. So, if a block builds on full.

14
00:01:54.970 --> 00:02:08.050
Potuz: It processes the request of the previous payload, and it performs specifically the state transition that would have been… would have happened on the payload, and then it continues processing its own state transition on the consensus side.

15
00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:15.249
Potuz: The problem is that, A request could include an exit for a builder.

16
00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:19.640
Potuz: And this is processed unconditionally.

17
00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:28.469
Potuz: And, Afterwards, we process the payments from the previous, payload.

18
00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:33.120
Potuz: So that's part of the state transition, because you just built on top of pool.

19
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:46.050
Potuz: So now, in a normal scenario, the situation is that, you process an exit for a builder, the exit is put there, and then you process, the payments, and…

20
00:02:46.050 --> 00:03:01.420
Potuz: the payments are either from the current EPOC or from the previous EPOC, if the block was there, and then you just… if there was a trustless payment, you just add a withdrawal for the… you add a withdrawal for the proposer.

21
00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.670
Potuz: Now, timings can be set in a very

22
00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:20.839
Potuz: specific way, if a lot of things have to happen, but it can be put up in a situation in which the withdrawal for the builder is put in the queue at the beginning of the processing, and then later, after that.

23
00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:29.060
Potuz: There's a withdrawal output for the proposer, also on the queue, and both of them are paid unconditionally on the.

24
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:36.469
Potuz: Both of them are paid unconditionally, if certain things happen. In that situation, the builder would be, minting money.

25
00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:44.800
Potuz: And there's a bunch of solutions that are possible for this. One of them is to not pay the proposer.

26
00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:52.580
Potuz: Another one is to burn, not only not pay the proposer, but actually burning that, that ETH.

27
00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:14.540
Potuz: Another one is to be careful with how to, what exit from the builder is, what's the withdrawal that is set for the builder. Be careful in the sense of, like, noticing that there might be in flight some payment for the proposers, and then deducting that from any potential exit from the builder.

28
00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:24.589
Potuz: And another one is to change the ordering, so perform first part of the consensus state transition, and then the request from the previous payload.

29
00:04:27.140 --> 00:04:32.129
Potuz: I personally prefer the simplest one, which is just not pay the proposer, and that's it.

